# generators-common

This package owns helpers used by more than one generator pack (`deterministic-reader`, `generate-context`, `generate-entry`, `fill`, `default-token`, `routes-api`, `routes-api-converter`, `casing-strategy`, `import-generator`, `settings`). YAML specification parsing lives under `src/parser/`. `yaml-node` is internal and is not a package export. Public parser API: `DeterministicParser(reader).parse(settings)` returns `IDeterministic` (`datasourceTypes`, `datasourceSeeds`, `viewTypes`, `expandedDatasourceTypes`, `expandedViewTypes`, `services`, `routes`); also export `IDeterministicReader`. No per-document parse methods. Expanded datasource types inject StandardTable columns (`id` unless a primary key is declared; `created`/`updated` and `uuid` unless `id_type` is uuid) using the same audit-column rules as SQL (no audit columns for readonly-lookup, or for custom-PK many-to-many; custom-PK otherwise follows optimistic concurrency) and keep `references`; a declared field named `id`, `created`, or `updated` is an error. Each expanded datasource type carries `primaryKeyColumn` and injected StandardTable columns whose `type` is already resolved (`id` from `datasource.id_type` / custom PK; `created`/`updated` as `datetime`). Expanded view types inline those inherited columns and drop enrichment FK columns. Language packs map `field.type` as-is — they must not add `idType` / `datetimeType` on the type object or recompute those from settings. Specification types stay on `specification`. The parser and routes-api IR are dialect-agnostic (YAML names, snake paths, `{param}`). HTTP param/segment casing for generated app code stays in each language pack. Identifier/file casing for generated app code goes through `createCasingStrategy` / pack `default-casing.ts`.

`IImportGenerator` is the shared path/include surface. Every method takes names (or emit files) and returns a `string`. Language packs own the concrete class and `createImportGenerator(basePath, settings)`. `other.organize_by_feature` is read only in that class constructor — never in generate-*.ts or `PackCasing`. Generators must not compose prefixes, `features/`, crate paths, or namespaces; they only call these methods. Do not add native type mapping (`type-converter` / `type-converters`) here; those stay in each language pack.

Language packs import this package directly. Do not copy these sources into pack `src/common/`.

`generate` is still the only export each language lane has. It takes `GenerateContext`: `{ reader, settings }` where `reader` is `{ read, exists }` (`IDeterministicReader`) and `settings` is the flat string dict.
